WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:11.693
In tutorial 11.1, you'll send alerts and
finished reports to the Slack or Microsoft

00:00:11.743 --> 00:00:14.508
Teams channel your team already watches.

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:19.456
First, open Company settings,
and choose the Integrations tab.

00:00:21.524 --> 00:00:24.326
Under Alerts and events,
click Add an endpoint.

00:00:27.053 --> 00:00:32.318
Next, choose where the messages go: a Slack
channel, or a Microsoft Teams channel.

00:00:33.524 --> 00:00:37.429
For Slack, type the channel's name,
then paste the webhook address,

00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:39.947
the private link Slack
gives you for that channel.

00:00:41.549 --> 00:00:45.199
Not sure where to find it? Show me how
walks you through getting it in Slack,

00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:46.346
step by step.

00:00:48.503 --> 00:00:52.913
Then pick the events this channel should
get, like finished reports, alerts,

00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:54.337
and big ranking moves.

00:00:55.503 --> 00:01:00.728
You can also send failed analyses,
reports held back, and new audit findings.

00:01:00.778 --> 00:01:04.453
Then choose which websites it
covers, or leave them clear for all,

00:01:04.503 --> 00:01:06.077
and click Add endpoint.

00:01:07.051 --> 00:01:10.536
Your channel now shows here,
with its events and website.

00:01:10.586 --> 00:01:13.660
Click Test, and a test message
arrives in the channel.

00:01:15.026 --> 00:01:18.076
The delivery log shows
every message that went out,

00:01:18.126 --> 00:01:21.244
and you can pause or remove
an endpoint at any time.

00:01:22.572 --> 00:01:26.832
So, add an endpoint, choose Slack
or Teams and paste the address,

00:01:26.882 --> 00:01:29.542
pick the events and
websites, and send a test.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:36.888
Your alerts now reach your team. Next, turn
findings into tickets, in tutorial 11.2.
